# Research Wiki Maintenance

**Constitution guardrails:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) §2 (source authority) + §3 (maintenance) · Wiki is **agent-native warm context** (navigation + accumulated knowledge); source wins.

## Read before substantial work

Research, labeling, review tooling, or non-trivial implementation:

- `docs/research_wiki/index.md`
- `docs/research_wiki/handoff.md`
- `docs/research_wiki/log.md` (tail)

**Query the wiki before re-deriving methodology** — check
`docs/research_wiki/concepts/` and `docs/research_wiki/reference/closed-questions.md` (do-not-re-run
registry) first. Maintenance is the agent's own investment: persist so the next agent orients in ms.

Truth: source docs, code, labels, experiment outputs, GitHub issues. When wiki and
evidence disagree, **source wins** — fix or flag the wiki
([source-authority.md](../../docs/research_wiki/reference/source-authority.md)).

## Update after meaningful work

Before final response when durable context was created:

- Smallest relevant page under `docs/research_wiki/`
- `index.md` if pages added/moved/retired
- One append to `log.md`
- `handoff.md` if focus, next action, blockers, or verification changed

Skip for trivial Q&A, status-only replies, or mechanical changes with no research context.

## Lint (keep memory consistent)

- **Mechanical (enforced):** `scripts/wiki_lint.py` (pre-commit; runs where links are authored —
  not CI, which would false-fail on local-only `archive/` paths) fails on dead internal links +
  orphan pages. Don't leave these to discipline.
- **Semantic (agent, periodic):** scan for stale claims, contradictions vs source, missing concept
  pages, wrong section/textual refs (e.g. a stale "§6"), superseded-not-marked. Fix or flag
  `> CONFLICT: …`, then log a `maintenance` entry. See `docs/research_wiki/README.md` "Lint".

## Guardrails

- Link to source docs; do not copy long specs into wiki.
- Search surface (`.rgignore`) stays scoped; knowledge corpus may grow (anti-runaway caps only).
- No promoting wiki notes to runtime behavior.
- No auto-fib, trading signals, edge claims, ML loops, or optimization via wiki.
- `*_candidate` ≠ human facit.
